(Now we need to ensure candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta true. We'll allocate beta to origin before processing origin, then after origin dispatch, vehicle_allocated may become false but candidate_vehicle_linked remains true (assuming not removed). So goal satisfied.)
(Now we need candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta true. We'll allocate beta to destination after origin dispatch (when beta becomes available). Then we will not dispatch destination, so vehicle_allocated remains true, candidate_vehicle_linked remains true. Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha true. We'll do prepare steps.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_task_profile_linked for both origin and destination to route_task_profile_alpha. We'll attach after vehicle allocated.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_node_ready and occupied, destination_node_ready and occupied. We'll activate nodes before loading, load payload, unload payload to get confirmed, but after unload we still have node ready (added) and occupied (unchanged). So we get both ready and occupied.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_availability_confirmed and locked true, destination_availability_confirmed and locked true. Load sets locked true, unload sets confirmed true.)
(Now we need to ensure transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_origin_linked to origin_node_alpha, transport_leg_destination_linked to destination_node_alpha, transport_leg_loading_authorized true. We'll assemble after both have loaded payload (locked true, confirmed false). Then authorize loading (requires origin_availability_locked true and candidate_task_profile_linked for origin). Then we can unload payloads to get confirmed true while keeping transport leg assembled and loading authorized.)
(Now we need to mark dispatch ready for origin and destination (requires transport leg assembled, loading authorized, lock, confirmed). After unload we have lock and confirmed true, transport leg assembled and loading authorized true. So we can mark dispatch ready for both.)
(Now we need to allocate dispatch slot to origin and destination. However we have only one dispatch slot. We'll need to allocate to origin, dispatch origin (which will make slot available again), then allocate to destination (but we will not dispatch destination). However after allocating to destination, we will not dispatch, so slot will stay allocated to destination (dispatch_allocated true). Goal requires dispatch_allocated destination_availability_alpha true, dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha true. That's fine. However after we allocate to origin and dispatch origin, slot becomes available again (due to dispatch effect). Then we allocate to destination (making slot allocated to destination). After that we will not dispatch destination, so slot remains allocated (dispatch_allocated true) and not available. Goal does not require dispatch_slot_available; it's fine.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha true (we will mark before allocation). After we mark dispatch ready origin, we allocate slot, then execute dispatch. After dispatch, dispatch_ready remains true? The effect of execute_origin_dispatch does not remove dispatch_ready. So dispatch_ready stays true. Good.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha true after allocation and remains true after dispatch (since not removed). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha true after marking and before allocation? Actually we need to mark dispatch ready destination before allocating slot (since allocate requires dispatch_ready true). We'll mark dispatch ready destination after we have transport leg assembled, loading authorized, lock, confirmed. Then we allocate slot to destination (since slot will be available after we dispatched origin). Then we will not execute dispatch destination, leaving dispatch_allocated true, dispatch_ready true.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_dispatch_slot_linked destination_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha true (from allocate action) and candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha true (from allocate action). After we allocate to origin then dispatch origin, the link remains (since not removed). After we allocate to destination, we will have both linked? Actually allocate action adds candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot. It does not remove previous links. So after allocating to origin, we have link origin-slot. After allocating to destination, we will have link destination-slot as well (in addition). So both will be true. Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha? Initially true. After we dispatch shift_candidate_alpha, does it remove the link? Not in effect. So shift_candidate_alpha will still be linked to slot. Goal does not require anything about shift_candidate_alpha's dispatch slot link. It's fine.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha remains true? Initially true. After dispatch shift_candidate_alpha, dispatch_allocated remains true (not removed). Goal requires dispatched shift_candidate_alpha true, dispatch_allocated? Not required. So fine.)
(Now we need to ensure compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha true. We'll release from shift_candidate_alpha early.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha? Not required in goal; we can release.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha remains true (it is already). No actions remove it.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_origin_availability_linked shift_candidate_alpha etc remain true (they are). Not removed.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_alpha etc remain true.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_alpha etc remain true.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha remains true (it is). Not removed.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha remains true (we won't remove). Fine.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_destination_availability_linked shift_candidate_beta destination_availability_alpha remains true (init true). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_origin_availability_linked shift_candidate_beta origin_availability_alpha remains true (init true). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta remains true (init true). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_operational_constraint_linked shift_candidate_beta operational_constraint_beta remains true (init true). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha remains true (init true). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta? Not required. Not in init. Not needed for goal. But some actions may require candidate_prepared for shift_candidate_beta? Not needed for goal. However we might need to allocate vehicle to shift_candidate_beta (requires candidate_created true, not vehicle_allocated, vehicle_available). That's fine.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha remains true (it is). Not needed to change.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha become true via confirm_candidate_preparedness.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha true (we will attach). Similarly for destination.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta true (we will allocate beta to origin before processing). After we allocate, we will have vehicle_allocated origin true, vehicle_available beta false, candidate_vehicle_linked origin beta true.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta true (we will allocate beta to destination after origin dispatch). After allocation, vehicle_allocated destination true, vehicle_available beta false, candidate_vehicle_linked destination beta true.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma true (we will allocate after shift_candidate_alpha dispatch). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha true (after origin dispatch). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true at goal? Not required but okay. After we load and unload both origins and destinations, cargo will be available (since each unload makes cargo available). However we load origin payload (cargo not available), unload origin (cargo available). Then load destination payload (cargo not available), unload destination (cargo available). So at end cargo available. Goal does not require cargo unavailable; fine.)
(Now we need to ensure loading_container_loaded? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure loading_container_leg_linked? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_staged_for_loading? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure equipment_reserved? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure equipment_confirmed? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure route_sequence_context_set? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure route_sequence_validated? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha? Already true.)
(Now we need to ensure constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha? Already true.)
(Now we need to ensure compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_alpha? Already true.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_availability_node_linked etc already true.)
(Now we need to ensure destination_availability_node_linked etc already true.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_node_ready and occupied after our sequence. We'll activate origin node (makes ready true, not occupied). Then load payload (makes occupied true, ready unchanged). Then unload payload (makes ready true (already true), confirmed true, cargo available). So after unload, we have origin_node_ready true, origin_node_occupied true. Good.)
(Now destination similar: activate destination node (makes ready true, not occupied). Load destination payload (makes occupied true, ready unchanged). Unload destination payload (makes ready true (already), confirmed true, cargo available). So after unload, destination_node_ready true, destination_node_occupied true.)
(Now we need to ensure transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha and transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha. The assemble_fully_loaded_leg will set those.)
(Now we need to ensure transport_leg_loading_authorized true. We'll authorize after assembly.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_availability_locked true and destination_availability_locked true. Load sets locked true; unload does not remove locked. So after load and before unload, locked true; after unload, locked still true.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_availability_confirmed true and destination_availability_confirmed true. Unload sets confirmed true.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha true and destination_availability_alpha true via mark actions.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha true and destination_availability_alpha true via allocate actions.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatched origin_availability_alpha true and dispatched shift_candidate_alpha true via execute actions.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatched destination_availability_alpha false? Not required but we will not dispatch.)
(Now we need to ensure dispatch_slot_available? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha? Not required but may be true after allocation (we will allocate beta to origin). After origin dispatch, vehicle_allocated may become false (if dispatch clears). Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true (we will allocate beta to destination before preparing destination? Actually we need vehicle allocated before preparing and attaching task profile. So we will allocate beta to destination after origin dispatch (when beta becomes available). Then we will prepare destination, attach task profile, etc. After that we will not dispatch destination, so vehicle_allocated remains true.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma true. We'll allocate after shift_candidate_alpha dispatch.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha true (after origin dispatch). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true (will be true after unloads). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha true (after release). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha false (after release). Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha remains true (it is). Not required to change.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha remains true (it will). Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha remains true (it is). Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma remains true (it is). Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_alpha transport_leg_alpha remains true (it is). Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure candidate_origin_availability_linked shift_candidate_alpha origin_availability_alpha remains true (it is). Not required.)
